"910MU", 6.36, 2.50,"R",75.00,"This Company binds the kind(s) of insurance stipulated on page 1 of this form. The Insurance is subject to the terms, conditions and"
"910MU", 7.22, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"limitations of the policy(ies) in current use by the Company."
"910MU", 8.86, 2.50,"R",75.00,"This binder may be cancelled by the Insured by surrender of this binder or by written notice to the Company stating when cancellation"
"910MU", 9.72, 2.50,"R",75.00,"will be effective. This binder may be cancelled by the Company by notice to the Insured in accordance with the policy conditions. This"
"910MU",10.58, 2.50,"R",75.00,"binder is cancelled when replaced by a policy. If this binder is not replaced by a policy, the Company is entitled to charge a premium"
"910MU",11.44, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"for the binder according to the Rules and Rates in use by the Company."
"910MU",14.86, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"Binders are effective for no more than ninety (90) days."
"910MU",17.86, 2.50,"R",75.00,"When this form is used to provide insurance in the amount of one million dollars ($1,000,000) or more, the title of the form is changed"
"910MU",18.72, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"from \"Insurance Binder\" to \"Cover Note\"."
"910MU",21.36, 2.50,"R",75.00,"With respect to binders issued to renters of residential premises, home owners, condo unit owners and mobile home owners, the"
"910MU",22.22, 2.50,"R",75.00,"insurer has thirty (30) business days, commencing from the effective date of coverage, to evaluate the issuance of the insurance"
"910MU",23.08, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"policy."
"910MU",25.86, 2.50,"R",75.00,"The mortgagee or Obligee of any mortgage or other instrument given for the purpose of creating a lien on real property shall accept as"
"910MU",26.72, 2.50,"R",75.00,"evidence of insurance a written binder issued by an authorized insurer or its agent if the binder includes or is accompanied by: the"
"910MU",27.58, 2.50,"R",75.00,"name and address of the borrower; the name and address of the lender as loss payee; a description of the insured real property; a"
"910MU",28.44, 2.50,"R",75.00,"provision that the binder may not be canceled within the term of the binder unless the lender and the insured borrower receive written"
"910MU",29.30, 2.50,"R",75.00,"notice of the cancellation at least ten (10) days prior to the cancellation; except in the case of a renewal of a policy subsequent to the"
"910MU",30.16, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"closing of the loan, a paid receipt of the full amount of the applicable premium, and the amount of insurance coverage."
"910MU",31.36, 2.50,"C",75.00,"Chapter 21 Title 25 Paragraph 2119"
"910MU",34.56, 2.50,"R",75.00,"Except for Auto Insurance coverage, no notice of cancellation or nonrenewal of a binder is required unless the duration of the binder"
"910MU",35.42, 2.50,"R",75.00,"exceeds 60 days. For auto insurance, the insurer must give 5 days prior notice, unless the binder is replaced by a policy or another"
"910MU",36.28, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"binder in the same company."
"910MU",38.86, 2.50,"R",75.00,"The insurer has 45 business days, commencing from the effective date of coverage to confirm eligibility for coverage under the"
"910MU",39.72, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"insurance policy."
"910MU",42.36, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"The policy may be cancelled at any time at the request of the insured."
"910MU",46.06, 2.50,"R",75.00,"No binder shall be valid beyond the issuance of the policy with respect to which it was given or beyond 90 days from its effective date,"
"910MU",46.92, 2.50,"R",75.00,"whichever period is the shorter.  If the policy has not been issued, a binder may be extended or renewed beyond such 90 days with the"
"910MU",47.78, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"written approval of the insurer."
"910MU",50.36, 2.50,"R",75.00,"Any person who refuses to accept a binder which provides coverage of less than $1,000,000.00 when proof is required: (A) Shall be"
"910MU",51.22, 2.50,"R",75.00,"fined not more than $500.00, and (B) is liable to the party presenting the binder as proof of insurance for actual damages sustained"
"910MU",52.08, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"therefrom."
"910MU",54.36, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"All policies shall expire at 12:01 a.m. standard time on the expiration date stated in the policy."
"910MU",57.61, 2.50,"R",75.00,"Binders are effective for no more than ninety (90) days.  A binder extension or renewal beyond such 90 days would require the written"
"910MU",58.47, 2.50,"L", 0.00,"approval by the Director of the Department of Consumer and Business Services."
